{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d1f85d96b1c5a8656350efead33c7527ca19d0712b0ce654985ec086a80318c5","digest":{"component_or_area":"JiraConfig validation and onboarding","key_entities":["JiraConfig","jira.url","jira.allow_insecure","jira.user","jira.project","InsecureUrlError","ConfigError","_validate_https_url","_validate_reconciler_tls","src/rebar/_config_schema.py","src/rebar/config.py","resolve_jira_settings","resolve_jira_datacenter_settings","write_jira_config","REBAR_JIRA_ALLOW_INSECURE","REBAR_RECONCILER_ALLOW_INSECURE","test_cloud_config_validation.py","test_config_jira_wiring.py","test_jira_onboard.py"],"problem_keywords":["cleartext credential exposure","https url validation","non-https rejection","jira config","scheme validation","insecure url","credential risk"],"propositions":["JiraConfig accepts non-https (http://) urls without validation, creating cleartext credential exposure risk unlike DC's ReconcilerConfig which rejects them","Config consumers in resolve_jira_settings and write_jira_config swallow ConfigError, allowing non-https urls to bypass validation silently","JiraConfig must gain a __post_init__ validator and allow_insecure flag to enforce https-only by default, with cleartext override only via explicit allow_insecure=true setting","The write path (write_jira_config) must validate and reject non-https urls before persisting, preventing the onboarding wizard from writing cleartext credentials to disk","resolve_jira_settings must re-raise InsecureUrlError before catching ConfigError to fail loud on deliberate non-https rejection while still degrades on malformed config"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354